title: context:set
tags: [[GUI command]] [[Event log]]
kind: reference
summary: Open a work context on the active repository: every later change is written in it

`context:set <name> [description]` opens a label named `name` — quoted when it has
spaces — described by the rest of the line, on the active repository, and every
change the GUI makes there afterwards — in any workspace on it — is written inside it,
until <<cmd "context:unset">>; the slot headers show it beside the repository's name.
Typed bare, it asks the name, then the description (empty for none). One at a time: setting another closes the first. It
survives a restart: opening the repository again asks whether to stay in it or end it
([[The GUI's work context]]).
